WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.670
Three ideas appear repeatedly A scalar subquery
behaves

00:00:05.683 --> 00:00:11.272
like one value A set subquery returns zero or more
values

00:00:11.561 --> 00:00:17.234
usually from one column A correlated subquery refers
to the current

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:22.934
outer row so its result can change as the outer row
changes When

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:27.842
you identify the shape and dependency the SQL
operator becomes easier to choose
